# 14. Measure integration success

## Regulatory and control measures

- supervisory commitments completed on time;
- unresolved regulatory findings;
- critical-control effectiveness;
- suspicious-activity and sanctions-alert quality;
- cyber incidents and recovery time;
- audit findings;
- regulatory-reporting accuracy.

## Technology measures

- critical-service availability;
- payment success rates;
- digital-app crash and abandonment rates;
- migration defects;
- reconciled balances;
- data-quality error rates;
- recovery-test performance;
- percentage of services using approved common interfaces.

## Customer measures

- customer retention;
- deposits and lending retention;
- complaints per 1,000 customers;
- complaint-resolution time;
- digital adoption;
- payment failures;
- branch and call-center service levels;
- customer trust and brand perception;
- access and inclusion outcomes.

## People and culture measures

- retention of critical employees;
- engagement by country and function;
- leadership turnover;
- completion of training;
- cross-country collaboration;
- control-escalation behavior;
- diversity of integration teams.

## Financial measures

- cost synergies realized;
- integration costs;
- revenue synergies;
- cost-to-income ratio;
- return on invested capital;
- customer lifetime value;
- technology run-cost reduction;
- losses avoided through improved fraud and controls.

